WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.005 --> 00:00:09.055
This is pi-switchboard. It picks the right model for every request in pi, subagents included, and keeps a receipt for each choice.

2
00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:19.610
pi is set to switchboard slash auto, a virtual model. Instead of one model for everything, every request is routed on its own.

3
00:00:20.214 --> 00:00:23.539
First, a small job: rename a function.

4
00:00:24.646 --> 00:00:37.096
A small classifier, running on this machine, reads the request in a fraction of a second. It answers three questions: what kind of work this is, how deep it goes, and how risky it is.

5
00:00:37.702 --> 00:00:47.277
The answer here is mechanical work, ninety-six percent sure. Your rules turn that into the light tier, so a small, cheap model does the job.

6
00:00:47.882 --> 00:00:52.607
Now some design work: a caching layer for the pricing API.

7
00:00:55.575 --> 00:01:03.450
The classifier calls this planning, and deep. Your rules send it to the deep tier, the strongest model in the profile.

8
00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:12.260
Next, the agent splits a review into three subagents that run in parallel: a scout, a worker and a reviewer.

9
00:01:13.951 --> 00:01:25.301
pi-switchboard classifies each child's task when it launches. The scout's quick search gets the light tier, the worker's coding gets standard, and the careful review gets deep.

10
00:01:26.518 --> 00:01:34.443
Control, Alt, W opens the navigator: every child, live, with its tier, its model and its tokens.

11
00:01:35.049 --> 00:01:48.349
Mid-task, the worker's account hits its usage limit. The whole account sits out until it resets, and the worker carries on with the next account in the same tier. Nobody has to retry by hand.

12
00:01:50.357 --> 00:02:02.932
Every choice has a receipt. Opening the worker shows why it ran where it did: the task as the classifier saw it, the answers with their confidence, and the rule that earned the standard tier.

13
00:02:03.545 --> 00:02:08.795
To install it, run the command on screen. Then start with slash tier tour.
